---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const title = 'Install WrenLore with Docker | WrenLore';
const description = 'Install WrenLore on your machine with Docker and one command. The installer generates secrets, pulls the public containers and waits for a healthy deployment.';
const command = 'curl -fsSL https://get.wrenlore.com/install.sh | bash';
const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'HowTo',
  name: 'Install WrenLore with Docker',
  description,
  totalTime: 'PT5M',
  tool: [{ '@type': 'HowToTool', name: 'Docker Engine with Docker Compose' }],
  step: [
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', name: 'Install Docker', text: 'Install and start Docker Engine with the Docker Compose plugin.' },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', name: 'Run the WrenLore installer', text: command },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', name: 'Open WrenLore', text: 'Open http://localhost:3000 in a browser.' },
  ],
};
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical="/install/" schema={schema}>
  <Header />
  <main>
    <section class="install-hero shell narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Docker installation</p>
      <h1>WrenLore, running locally.<br />One command.</h1>
      <p class="install-lede">Bring a working Docker environment. WrenLore handles the deployment, credentials and health checks.</p>

      <div class="install-command" data-install-command>
        <code>{command}</code>
        <button type="button" data-copy-command aria-label="Copy installation command">Copy</button>
      </div>
      <p class="command-note">No account, licence key or hand-edited <code>.env</code> file.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="install-demo shell">
      <div class="terminal-frame">
        <div class="terminal-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><b>WrenLore installation</b></div>
        <img src="/screenshots/wrenlore-install.gif" alt="Terminal recording of the WrenLore installer pulling its Docker images and reporting a healthy installation at localhost port 3000" loading="eager" />
      </div>
      <p>A real clean installation recorded on Kobe. Download time depends on your connection.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="agent-install-method shell narrow">
      <div>
        <h2>Prefer to hand the installation to an agent?</h2>
        <p>Use the same public installer with a bounded prompt that checks Docker, protects existing deployments and verifies health without printing secrets.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="https://github.com/wrenlore/wrenlore/blob/master/docs/AGENT_INSTALL.md">Open the agent installation guide →</a>
    </section>

    <section class="section shell narrow install-steps">
      <div class="section-heading compact"><p class="eyebrow">Before you begin</p><h2>Docker is the only prerequisite.</h2></div>
      <p>Install and start Docker Engine with the Docker Compose plugin. Your user must be able to run <code>docker</code> without changing privileges inside the installer.</p>
      <div class="docker-links">
        <a href="https://docs.docker.com/desktop/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>macOS or Windows</strong><span>Install Docker Desktop →</span></a>
        <a href="https://docs.docker.com/engine/install/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Linux</strong><span>Install Docker Engine →</span></a>
        <a href="https://docs.docker.com/compose/install/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Already use Docker?</strong><span>Check Docker Compose →</span></a>
      </div>

      <div class="numbered-step"><span>1</span><div><h2>Run the installer</h2><p>Open a terminal and paste:</p><div class="install-command install-command-small"><code>{command}</code></div></div></div>
      <div class="numbered-step"><span>2</span><div><h2>Open WrenLore</h2><p>When the installer reports that WrenLore is ready, open <a href="http://localhost:3000"><code>http://localhost:3000</code></a>.</p></div></div>
      <div class="numbered-step"><span>3</span><div><h2>Create the first account</h2><p>Complete the setup in your browser. The local WrenLore stack remains on your machine.</p></div></div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-ink"><div class="shell narrow install-details">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">What the command does</p><h2>The boring setup work, automated.</h2></div>
      <ul>
        <li>Checks that Docker Engine and Docker Compose are available.</li>
        <li>Creates an isolated installation under <code>~/.wrenlore</code>.</li>
        <li>Generates strong application and database secrets automatically.</li>
        <li>Pulls WrenLore from public GHCR, plus PostgreSQL/pgvector and Redis.</li>
        <li>Starts the stack and waits until the application is healthy.</li>
        <li>Preserves secrets and persistent data when the installer is run again.</li>
      </ul>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section shell narrow install-options">
      <div class="section-heading compact"><p class="eyebrow">Useful options</p><h2>Defaults first. Control when you need it.</h2></div>
      <div class="option-row"><code>--port 3001</code><span>Use another local port if 3000 is occupied.</span></div>
      <div class="option-row"><code>--version 0.1.12</code><span>Pin a specific WrenLore image version.</span></div>
      <div class="option-row"><code>--dir /path/to/wrenlore</code><span>Choose another installation directory.</span></div>
      <div class="option-row"><code>--app-url https://wiki.example.com</code><span>Set the public URL when deploying behind your own proxy.</span></div>
      <p class="runbook-note">Need TLS, backups, reverse proxy configuration or production operations? Continue to the <a href="https://github.com/wrenlore/wrenlore/blob/master/README-deploy.md">operator runbook</a> after the basic installation.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-copy-command]').forEach((button) => {
    button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      const command = button.closest('[data-install-command]')?.querySelector('code')?.textContent?.trim();
      if (!command) return;
      await navigator.clipboard.writeText(command);
      const original = button.textContent;
      button.textContent = 'Copied';
      window.setTimeout(() => { button.textContent = original; }, 1600);
    });
  });
</script>
